<title>UK: ICL to supply smartcards for London tube - report.</title>
<headline>ICL to supply smartcards for London tube - report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>A consortium led by ICL and EDS will be awarded  a project to introduce 'smartcard' tickets on the London bus and underground  network, The Times reported on Friday.</p>
<p>The award of the contract, part of the British government's Private  Finance Initiative (PFI), is believed to be worth 500 million stg,  the report said.</p>
<p>The ICL/EDS team, called TranSys, also includes Cubic Corporation  and WS Atkins. It plans to replace paper train and underground tickets  with smartcards which open barriers automatically.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
